From e961773a6afbaa737b5de285e40b610a1d369216 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:45:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/49] Replace manual stream test with live room features in
 the dock

The dock's lower half becomes a live-room area: stats (watched, likes,
high-energy count, danmaku status), a danmaku tab with the live feed
(chat, gifts, Super Chats, guards, entries/follows), sending and
read-aloud, and a room tab for editing the title. The manual RTMP test
remains available only through the automation vendor.

The Swift core adds the danmaku protocol (packets, zlib/brotli,
INTERACT_WORD_V2 protobuf, WBI signing), a reconnecting DanmakuClient
that follows the ready account's room, send-danmaku and title update
requests, and a short-queue speaker. The Go live status now warns when a
stream started by Go live stops outside End live while the room stays
open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
